  "notes": "Warren J. Smith, Modern Lens Design, 2nd ed., Figure 20.3 (zoom), p. 380. Multi-configuration model: configuration 1 = short, 2 = mid, 3 = long. Book values by configuration: [short] Figure 20.3 short, p. 380. Book: EFL 57.14, BFL 28.61, NA -0.1787 (F/2.8), GIH 15.43 (HFOV=15.11), PTZ/F -20.19, VL 137.91, infinite conjugate. [mid] Figure 20.3 mid, p. 381. Book: EFL 99.99, BFL 28.61, NA -0.1787 (F/2.8), GIH 15.4 (HFOV=8.75), PTZ/F -11.51, VL 137.91, infinite conjugate. [long] Figure 20.3 long, p. 382. Book: EFL 142.8, BFL 28.61, NA -0.1787 (F/2.8), GIH 15.43 (HFOV=6.16), PTZ/F -8.08, VL 137.91, infinite conjugate. [end] Glass: LAK8 entered as N-LAK8; NBK7 entered as N-BK7 (517/642); NLAF9 entered as LAF9 (Schott LAF9, 795/284 as in the book); NLASF entered as N-LAF34 (Schott 773/496; the book gives 773/497); NLK1 entered as LACL7 (Hoya LACL7, 670/573; the book gives 670/575); SK11 entered as N-SK11; SK5 entered as N-SK5. Stop at surface 18 (the book's plane air surface). Zoom lens: the configurations are the zoom positions the book lists (short, mid, long); the per-position files Figure 20.3 short/mid/long.lens.json hold the same data one position per file. The multi-configuration table sets APER, YFIE 1, YFIE 2, THIC 5, THIC 10, THIC 13. Discrepancy with the book: the model EFL is about 0.1 % long and the back focus 0.05 long in every zoom position, which no glass within the book's rounded indices explains; since the error scales with EFL it most likely sits in the fixed rear group (surfaces 14 to 22), perhaps a misprinted digit.",
